#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# diagonalizable_matrix_q

#% text
# `diagonalizable_matrix_q(m)` gives true when the exact square matrix m is diagonalizable over the complex numbers.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The test: the square-free part s = p/gcd(p, p') of the characteristic polynomial p annihilates m exactly when the minimal polynomial of m has no repeated factor (Horn and Johnson, Matrix Analysis, 3.3). Matrices with inexact entries stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
diagonalizable_matrix_q([[1, 1], [0, 1]])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
diagonalizable_matrix_q([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
diagonalizable_matrix_q([[2, 0], [0, 2]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
diagonalizable_matrix_q([[0, -1], [1, 0]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
diagonalizable_matrix_q([[6, 0, 0], [0, 12, 1], [0, 0, 12]])
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
